  "final_text": "Both items exist and the rule is enabled. The dashboard is titled \"EFF-2619d3a7 Web logs overview\" and has four panels. The rule is \"EFF-2619d3a7 5xx spike\".\n\n**Dashboard** (ID `9ae0c0c8-5556-420f-8ff8-1e95791871aa`), built on the `kibana_sample_data_logs` data view:\n- **Total requests**: count of all requests.\n- **5xx responses**: count filtered to `response.keyword` from 500 to 599.\n- **Unique client IPs**: unique count of `clientip`.\n- **Requests over time**: line chart of request counts per time bucket.\n\n**Rule** (ID `76857b7b-6848-4194-b460-3cef772c0c70`):\n- Type: Elasticsearch query (`.es-query`), KQL search-source form.\n- Query: `response.keyword >= \"500\" and response.keyword <= \"599\"`, count aggregation over the last 5 minutes.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10. Checks every 1 minute.\n- Enabled. The first run succeeded with 0 alerts.\n- I didn't add a notification action, since you didn't ask for one.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- Treated \"5xx\" as response codes 500\u2013599, matched as a range on the keyword field of `response`.\n- Added a `consumer` of `alerts` and a `EFF-2619d3a7` tag on the rule, to make it easy to find.\n\n**Limits:**\n- I didn't profile the values in `response`. The Kibana console, internal search and ES|QL endpoints are disabled in this setup, and Elasticsearch isn't reachable directly. So I haven't confirmed that the 5xx filter matches any documents in this data.\n- The data view's field list was the only exploration I could do.",
